<div class="wrap page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">Upper Years · 14 to 18 years</p>
  <h1>Your own pace, with a coach in the room</h1>
  <p class="lede">Upper Years students work toward a US high school diploma or a Cambridge pathway through accredited online courses, with our teachers coaching them daily. Alongside that: exam preparation, a personal project, and one trip a year that the students plan and budget themselves.</p>
</div>

<section class="band--paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Two pathways</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>US diploma</h3>
        <p>An online high school program accredited in the US, leading to a diploma recognised by the US Department of Education. Students move through courses at their own pace with a PRA teacher tracking progress and unblocking them every day.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Cambridge pathway</h3>
        <p>For students aiming at UK-style university admission. Cambridge-backed courses toward IGCSE and beyond, supported by our subject teachers.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="form__note">Not sure which fits? That is what the first conversation is for. <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">Ask us.</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{% set riverColor = "var(--sand)" %}{% include "partials/river.njk" %}

<section>
  <div class="wrap two">
    <div>
      <h2>Exams we prepare for</h2>
      <p><strong>IELTS</strong> and <strong>Pearson PTE</strong> for English proficiency, which most universities abroad ask for. <strong>GED</strong> for students who want a recognised secondary credential on a faster route. Targeted coaching, practice papers, and a plan for each student, not a generic class.</p>
      <h2>The personal project</h2>
      <p>Every student owns one project for the year. It can be a business, a piece of research, a film, an app, a garden. They set the goal, we hold them to it, and they present the result. It is the thing they will talk about in university interviews.</p>
      <h2>The trip</h2>
      <p>Once a year the Upper Years plan an educational trip: destination, budget, itinerary, logistics. They do the spreadsheets. We check them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="photo photo--blob photo--portrait" data-caption="photo: an Upper Years student presenting their project, or the trip"></div>
  </div>
</section>

